      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "τὰ δὲ ἀπόγεια τῶν χειμάρρων καὶ τὰ φυσήματα",
          "english_quote": "the winds blowing from land during the storms, and the gusts",
          "issue": "χειμάρρων ordinarily points to torrents or winter-swollen streams, not simply to storms. The draft also turns the genitive relationship into the temporal claim “during the storms.” Its note acknowledges difficulty but does not establish either substitution. The compressed expression remains difficult; that difficulty does not authorize silently treating χειμάρρων as a form of χειμών.",
          "suggested_revision": "Rework this phrase while preserving its unresolved relationship. A source-transparent candidate for fresh review is “the offshore winds of the torrents, and the gusts,” with a note explaining that “of the torrents” represents the supplied genitive and that its precise nautical sense is uncertain. Investigate the lexical and contextual relationship before adopting a smoother interpretation; do not change the Greek or import another edition’s wording.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "15",
      "verdict": "blocked",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": false,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "οἱ πρεσβύτεροι ὥσπερ ’ναῦται καταρτιζέτωσαν ἐπιμελῶς -ὰ χρῄζοντα ἑκάστῳ.",
          "english_quote": "The elders, like sailors, should carefully prepare what each person needs.",
          "issue": "The supplied sequence “-ὰ” remains unresolved, while the translation proceeds on the proposed reading “τὰ χρῄζοντα.” The note distinguishes its proposal from the supplied reading, but its argument that χρῄζοντα lacks an expected article does not itself prove corruption: an article is not invariably required for a substantival participle. The image check establishes the printed form, not the function of the mark or the validity of a reconstruction. Coverage and lexical fidelity cannot be certified for this locus.",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep the passage blocked pending examination of the relevant print evidence, Lagarde’s typographic conventions, and any applicable apparatus. Determine whether “-ὰ” represents editorial notation, a damaged or defective printed sequence, or something else. If an actual source defect is established, obtain the necessary textual evidence before adopting a correction. Preserve “-ὰ χρῄζοντα” as supplied and label “τὰ χρῄζοντα” only as a proposed correction. Any resulting English must undergo fresh review.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ὥσπερ ’ναῦται",
          "english_quote": "No elision is expected there, so the mark appears to be a typographical feature rather than part of the word.",
          "issue": "The absence of expected elision supports distinguishing the prefix mark from the lexical word, but it does not determine whether the mark is accidental or intentional editorial notation. The proposed unmarked reading should not be treated as an established correction to the image-checked print.",
          "suggested_revision": "In source_issues, retain the exact supplied “ὥσπερ ’ναῦται” and describe the mark as a printed feature whose editorial function requires clarification. Do not diagnose an OCR error or delete it from the source transcription merely because it is not an elision mark.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ὡς πρωρεὺς ’ἐγρηγορὼς",
          "english_quote": "The participle is syntactically complete without it, and no elision accounts for the mark.",
          "issue": "Syntactic completeness does not establish that the prefix mark is a printing mistake. As with the mark before ναῦται, its possible editorial function must be distinguished from genuine corruption.",
          "suggested_revision": "Preserve “ὡς πρωρεὺς ’ἐγρηγορὼς” in the transcription. Clarify the edition’s notation before presenting the unmarked form as a correction; record this separately from the unresolved “-ὰ” locus.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τοῦ κυβερνήτου μόνου τοὺς λόγους ἀντιβαλλέτω",
          "english_quote": "The bishop, like a bow officer keeping watch, should relay only the helmsman’s words.",
          "issue": "μόνου modifies κυβερνήτου: the exclusivity concerns the helmsman as the source. The English placement of “only” can instead emphasize words rather than other things the helmsman supplies. The intended reading is recoverable, but the source’s focus can be preserved more clearly.",
          "suggested_revision": "For fresh review: “The bishop, like a bow officer keeping watch, should relay the words of the helmsman alone.” This wording proposal does not resolve the passage’s blocking source issue.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
